---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="About this AstroPublishKit demo site.">
  <article class="shell prose standalone-prose">
    <h1>About this starter</h1>
    <p>AstroPublishKit is a static-first publishing foundation. Replace this page, change the site configuration, and start writing.</p>
    <h2>What belongs in the kit</h2>
    <p>Content structure, discoverability, search, quality checks and deployment defaults belong here. Your brand, editorial voice and production analytics identifiers do not.</p>
    <h2>Where to customize</h2>
    <p>Start with <code>astro-publish-kit.config.mjs</code>, then adjust <code>src/styles/global.css</code> if you want a different visual system.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
